<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diploma Andreanum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1224</span> · Also known as Andreanum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Diploma Andreanum was a charter issued by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-ii-of-hungary">Andrew II of Hungary</a> in 1224 granting collective privileges to the German 'guests', the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvanian-saxons">Transylvanian Saxons</a>, settled around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sibiu">Hermannstadt</a> (Sibiu). It gave them their own count, judges and freely elected priests, freedom of trade and a fixed tax in return for military service, and it remained the basis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> autonomy until 1876.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diploma-andreanum.jpg" alt="Diploma Andreanum" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Siebenbürgisch-Sächsische Stiftung · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Goldener_freibrief_1224.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
